\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. No, not despairingly
\par Come I to Thee;
\par No, not distrustingly
\par Bend I the knee:
\par Sin hath gone over me,
\par Yet is this still my plea:
\par Jesus hath died.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Ah! mine iniquity
\par Crimson has been,
\par Infinite, infinite,
\par Sin upon sin;
\par Sin of not loving Thee,
\par Sin of not trusting Thee,
\par Infinite sin.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Lord! I confess to Thee
\par Sadly my sin;
\par All I am tell I Thee,
\par All I have been:
\par Purge Thou my sin away,
\par Wash Thou muy soul this day;
\par Lord, make me clean.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Faithful and just art Thou,
\par Forgiving all;
\par Loving and kind art thou
\par When poor ones call:
\par Lord, let the cleansing blood,
\par Blood of the Lamb of God,
\par Pass o'er  my soul.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Then all is peace and light
\par This soul within;
\par Thus shall I walk with Thee,
\par The loved Unseen;
\par Leaning on Thee, my God,
\par Guided along the road,
\par Nothing between.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

